cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "GLO-NCA: Global Context-Aware Neural Cellular Automata for Brain Tumor Segmentation"
abstract: >-
  A lightweight, global-context-aware Neural Cellular Automata (NCA) architecture
  for multi-modal 3D brain-tumor segmentation on BraTS. GLO-NCA is a unified
  two-level model on a 128^3 working volume: a global-context level at 48^3 and a
  segmentation level at 64^3 (30 NCA steps in total), with squeeze-and-excitation
  channel attention and spatial global context at every NCA step, learnable
  cross-level projections and a learned fusion. The production model has 30,209
  inference parameters (30,284 during training, including 75 deep-supervision
  auxiliary parameters).
type: software
